# Model Context Protocol Servers (`modelcontextprotocol/servers`)

The official **Model Context Protocol (MCP)** reference server collection (`74,200+` GitHub stars), providing standardized JSON-RPC tool integrations for GitHub, Git, filesystem operations, and databases.

> **Standardized Tooling:** MCP servers expose strongly typed resources, prompts, and execution tools over `stdio` or Server-Sent Events (`SSE`).

## One-Line Server Launch

```bash
npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/server-github
```

## Configuration Example (`mcp.json`)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_token": "<YOUR_TOKEN>"
      }
    },
    "filesystem": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "./workspace"]
    }
  }
}
```

## Most Used Official MCP Servers

| Package | Category | Primary Capabilities |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-github` | `API` | Repository search, PR management, issue triage, file commits |
| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-git` | `CLI` | Local Git log inspection, diff generation, branch switching |
| `@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres` | `API` | Read-only schema inspection and parameterized SQL queries |
